class.description:
A dialogue choice node offers the player a list of [member options]. It has the flow input [code]in[/code] and one flow output per option, named by [method get_option_port].
At runtime the node waits ([constant FlowGraphPlayback.ENTER_RESULT_WAIT]). The dialogue UI reads the options with [method FlowGraphPlayback.get_available_exits]: one [FlowExit] per option, in the order of [member options], with the translated option text as label. An option is disabled ([member FlowExit.enabled] is [code]false[/code]) when its [member DialogueOption.condition] is false or when it is a [member DialogueOption.once] option that was already taken in this run. The UI hides or grays out disabled options and calls [method FlowGraphPlayback.choose] with the index of the chosen one. [method FlowGraphPlayback.advance] takes the first enabled option.
Taken [member DialogueOption.once] options are stored in the node memory of the playback, so they are part of [FlowGraphState] and are forgotten when the graph is started again. To hide an option for the whole savegame, set a variable when it is taken and test it in the condition.
If every option has a condition or is shown once, the node shows a configuration warning: when none is available, the dialogue can't continue. Add an option without a condition as a fallback.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func show_choices() -> void:
	var exits := playback.get_available_exits()
	for i in exits.size():
		var button := Button.new()
		button.text = exits[i].label
		button.disabled = not exits[i].enabled
		button.pressed.connect(playback.choose.bind(i))
		choice_box.add_child(button)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private void ShowChoices()
{
	var exits = _playback.GetAvailableExits();
	for (int i = 0; i < exits.Count; i++)
	{
		int index = i;
		var button = new Button { Text = exits[i].Label, Disabled = !exits[i].Enabled };
		button.Pressed += () => _playback.Choose(index);
		_choiceBox.AddChild(button);
	}
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
